          "text": "The pattern indexes as a primitive hexagonal cell with \\(a \\approx 3.7516\\) \u00c5 and \\(c \\approx 12.480\\) \u00c5. The \\(00l\\) condition \\(l=2n\\), together with the intensity distribution, supports the 2H-delafossite-type space group \\(P6_3/mmc\\) (No. 194), \\(Z=2\\).\n\nPb occupies the octahedral 2a site, Au the linearly coordinated 2c site, and O the 4f site with \\(z\\approx0.090\\). The oxygen coordinate is less precisely determined than the lattice parameters because Pb and Au dominate the Cu-radiation intensities.\n\n### Primary CIF\n\n```cif\ndata_PbAuO2_primary\n_audit_creation_method              'Indexed and fitted from supplied Cu Kalpha1 powder pattern'\n_chemical_name_common               'lead gold dioxide'\n_chemical_formula_structural        'PbAuO2'\n_chemical_formula_sum               'Pb1 Au1 O2'\n_chemical_formula_weight            436.16\n\n_cell_length_a                      3.7516\n_cell_length_b                      3.7516\n_cell_length_c                     12.480\n_cell_angle_alpha                  90\n_cell_angle_beta                   90\n_cell_angle_gamma                 120\n_cell_volume                       152.11\n_cell_formula_units_Z                2\n\n_space_group_name_H-M_alt          'P 63/m m c'\n_space_group_IT_number             194\n\n_exptl_crystal_density_diffrn        9.52\n_diffrn_radiation_type             'Cu Kalpha1'\n_diffrn_radiation_wavelength         1.5406\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_symmetry_multiplicity\n_atom_site_Wyckoff_symbol\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\n_atom_site_occupancy\nPb1  Pb  2  a  0.000000  0.000000  0.000000  1.0\nAu1  Au  2  c  0.333333  0.666667  0.250000  1.0\nO1   O   4  f  0.333333  0.666667  0.090000  1.0\n```\n\nRepresentative indexing is:\n\n| Observed \\(2\\theta\\) | hkl |\n|---:|:---|\n| 14.18\u00b0 | 002 |\n| 27.43\u00b0 | 100 |\n| 28.37\u00b0 | 101 |\n| 28.57\u00b0 | 004 |\n| 31.01\u00